cl inlines every local class and every closure in this case away and emits no symbol for any of them; cxx1 has no COMDAT and no way to say a definition is mergeable, so it emits a real function for each constructor, destructor and call operator. Every difference is a name cxx1 has and cl has none of - the same divergence local-class.nocl and lambda.nocl record, and docs/CONFORMANCE.md under "An inline member function is a strong symbol". What this case exists to check is visible in those names rather than in the count, and it agrees: cxx1 writes ??0L@?1??one@@YAHXZ@QEAA@XZ and ??0L@?1??two@@YAHXZ@QEAA@XZ, two symbols for two types, each carrying its own enclosing function. Before this fix both were ??0L@@QEAA@XZ and the assembler refused the second definition, which is the bug the case is named for.
